  "query_preview": "(Monday through Wednesday)...\nA closed upper-level low over the West Coast will dig \nsoutheastward into the Central Plains on Monday, inducing \nsurface cyclogenesis over Colorado and Kansas. The upper low is \nprojected to stall and slowly meander eastward across the \nmid/lower Mississippi Valley through midweek. While timing \ndifferences between the models persist, mild temperatures in \nthe 70s and periodic shower/thunderstorm chances will dominate \nearly to midweek. A strong cold front trailing the surface low \nlate in the week will usher in a significantly cooler airmass, \ndropping high temperatures into the 40s and 50s. Given timing \ndiscrepancies among models, the NBM currently broad-brushes the \nthermal gradient late in the week averaging out the forecast \nhighs in the 60s.",
